## Event Schema

```java
// ✅ Events are immutable records with all required metadata
public record PipelineCreatedEvent(
    @NotNull UUID eventId,           // Unique event ID for idempotency
    @NotNull UUID pipelineId,
    @NotNull UUID tenantId,
    @NotNull String name,
    @NotNull Instant occurredAt,
    @NotNull String eventType        // "pravah.pipeline.created"
) implements DomainEvent {}

// Event type naming: {domain}.{entity}.{action}
// Examples: pravah.pipeline.created, pravah.execution.completed, pravah.job.failed
```

## Outbox Pattern (MANDATORY)

```java
// ✅ Never publish directly to Kafka from business logic
@Transactional
public Pipeline createPipeline(CreatePipelineCommand cmd) {
    Pipeline pipeline = Pipeline.create(cmd);
    pipelineRepository.save(pipeline);
    
    // Write to outbox in SAME transaction
    outboxRepository.save(new OutboxEntry(
        UUID.randomUUID(),
        "pravah.pipeline.events",
        pipeline.getId().toString(),  // Key for partitioning
        serialize(new PipelineCreatedEvent(...)),
        Instant.now()
    ));
    
    return pipeline;  // Kafka publish happens async via OutboxPublisher
}

// ❌ NEVER do this - dual write problem
pipeline = pipelineRepository.save(pipeline);
kafkaTemplate.send("topic", event);  // If this fails, DB is committed but event lost
```

## Idempotent Consumer (MANDATORY)

```java
@KafkaListener(topics = "pravah.pipeline.events", groupId = "execution-service")
public void handlePipelineEvent(PipelineEvent event) {
    // ✅ Check if already processed
    if (processedEventRepository.existsById(event.eventId())) {
        log.info("Duplicate event, skipping", kv("eventId", event.eventId()));
        return;
    }
    
    // Process the event
    processEvent(event);
    
    // Mark as processed in SAME transaction
    processedEventRepository.save(new ProcessedEvent(event.eventId(), Instant.now()));
}
```

## Consumer Configuration

```java
@Configuration
public class KafkaConsumerConfig {
    @Bean
    public ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory<String, String> kafkaListenerContainerFactory() {
        var factory = new ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory<String, String>();
        factory.setConsumerFactory(consumerFactory());
        
        // ✅ Manual ack for exactly-once
        factory.getContainerProperties().setAckMode(AckMode.MANUAL);
        
        // ✅ Error handling with DLT
        factory.setCommonErrorHandler(new DefaultErrorHandler(
            new DeadLetterPublishingRecoverer(kafkaTemplate),
            new FixedBackOff(1000L, 3)  // 3 retries, 1s apart
        ));
        
        return factory;
    }
}
```

## Topic Naming

```
pravah.{service}.{entity}.events   → Domain events
pravah.{service}.{entity}.commands → Commands
pravah.{topic}.DLT                 → Dead letter topic
```

## Partition Key Strategy

| Event Type | Key | Reason |
|------------|-----|--------|
| Pipeline events | pipelineId | Same pipeline events in order |
| Execution events | executionId | Execution lifecycle in order |
| Job events | executionId | All jobs for execution together |
